<title>FRANCE: Credit Lyonnais cuts base rate.</title>
<headline>Credit Lyonnais cuts base rate.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>French bank Credit Lyonnais said on Monday it was cutting its base lending rate to 6.30 percent from 6.55 percent effective December 18.</p>
<p>The move followed identical moves by most of France's other major commercial banks.</p>
<p>The banks last cut base lending rate, at which they lend to their best customers, on September 20.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5452</p>
